<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Socotra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Socotra is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a>, belonging to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. Its long isolation produced a unique flora, including the dragon's blood tree, and the archipelago became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2008. Known to ancient traders for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> and aloes, it was held by the Portuguese from 1507 to 1511 and ruled by the Mahra sultans until 1967.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/socotra.jpg" alt="Socotra" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socotra_satview.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
